  "scenario": "A long-time membrane or laptop-keyboard user is considering a first mechanical keyboard and wants to understand what physically causes a keypress to register, what red, brown, blue, and other switch colors can and cannot tell them, and how to choose a first board for their own layout, connection, noise, and feel requirements. The available material contains membrane-contact and keyboard-matrix references, a Cherry MX family reference, four current catalog snapshots using several layouts and switch labels, and four community discussions with conflicting experiences. It does not contain a controlled membrane-versus-mechanical performance trial, a cross-manufacturer switch-color standard, or hands-on results for this buyer.",
